**How to implement.** Stages 2 and 3 of the reference pipeline join stage 1 in `StagedMuellerPath`, and the section 7.2 fact keeps only its assertions (001 §Q AT-1 '… `familyGain`, `correctSignal`, `buildDesign`, `reconstruct`) is promoted into product code as the study's staged Mueller path, and §7.2 is re-pointed to call it'; 001 §S10 third bullet; the S10.3 brief 'It returns typed stage-1 constants, the reconstructed matrices with rank and residual' and 'sec 7.2 calls the promoted path, and its body keeps only assertions'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §6 row '§7.2 pipeline: `MuellerReconstructionTests` §7.2 → product staged path', deleted at the source: 'The hand-composed body'): after the step the hand-composed Stage 3 exists once, in product code. (1) In `StagedMuellerPath.fs` (step 349): (a) `StagedMuellerError` gains `ObjectReconstructionErr of kind : MatrixKind * error : SolverError` (the stage-3 solve of that object failed; `MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixKind`). (b) After `calibrateStageOne`, `StagedMuellerData = { stageOne : StageOneCalibrationData; gains : GainCalibration; cplCplDay1Gain : InterpolatedGain; qz : ReconstructedMatrix; lr : ReconstructedMatrix; qzLr : ReconstructedMatrix }`, doc one to three lines: the stage-1 constants, the AIR gain rules (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:GainCalibration`, whose `cplCpl` is the day-2 `Day2Single`), the day-1 CPL-CPL interpolation (`:InterpolatedGain`), and M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} with their rank and residual (`:ReconstructedMatrix`). (c) `reconstructStaged (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) (excluded : ExcludedPoint list) (captures : StagedMuellerCaptureData) : Result<StagedMuellerData, StagedMuellerError>`, the rest of today's section 7.2 body moved with its rules and values, in this order: `calibrateStageOne`, its error passing through; the CPL-LP split time, the earliest `capturedAt` of `bullshitCheckRows` (the reference `assign_gain_model` reads the first check), no row answering `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming the bullshit checks; the nine AIR blocks, each the rows of its file whose `experiment` equals its label, in this order: `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2` and `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R` of `lpLpRows`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2` and `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2R` of `lpCplRows`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2R` of `cplLpRows`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR` of `cplCplDay1Rows` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2` of `cplCplDay2Rows` (the labels `assign_gain_model` selects, `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_fit_linear.py:94-144`), the first block with no row answering `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming its label, where the fact divides 0 by 0 or throws today; each block's gain by the fact's `fitAirGain` and the day-1 block times by its `meanTime`, with the sources (`LpSource`, `stageOne.cplSource`) and analyzers (`stageOne.lpAnalyzer`, `stageOne.cplAnalyzer`) its `calibration` and `day1Cal` use; the five families' projections as its `prepareRow` and `families` build them, in step 350's form; and, for `Qz`, `Lr` and `QzLrProduct` in that order, the five families' `buildDesign` systems over `excluded`, concatenated in family order and solved by `reconstruct`, the first failure answering `ObjectReconstructionErr` with the kind and the `SolverError`. The nine labels are literals of the path, born as `MuellerExperimentLabel`s: they are the reference procedure's gain rules, which S11.1 turns into session data (001 §L 'familyGain becomes their first implementation'). The excluded points are the caller's data (spec 0042 §0; 001 §Q AT-1 'the excluded frame [is] applied as data'). Helpers are private or local and meet ELEV003P, ELEV010P and ELEV013. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs` gains, after the cascade values, the nine AIR gains of `reference_step2_linear_summary.json`'s `gain_summary`, each an `AirGain` with a one-line doc naming its key: `lpLpGainA` 45028.89958338373 (`lp_lp.gain_air2`), `lpLpGainB` 44514.55313613668 (`lp_lp.gain_air2r`), `lpCplGainA` 64241.39738340334 (`lp_cpl.gain_air2`), `lpCplGainB` 63009.84001492676 (`lp_cpl.gain_air2r`), `cplLpGainPre` 36886.57620207925 (`cpl_lp.gain_pre_air2`), `cplLpGainPost` 40015.20947516168 (`cpl_lp.gain_post_air2r`), `cplCplDay1GainStart` 34623.69085844701 and `cplCplDay1GainEnd` 37056.15607055087 (`cpl_cpl_day1.gain_start`, `.gain_end`) and `cplCplDay2Gain` 36225.080943100205 (`cpl_cpl_day2.gain`). `dataMatrixTol`'s doc gains one line: it also bands the AIR gains, whose worst observed deviation was 2.9e-11 (`lp_cpl.gain_air2`) when spec 0050 was authored, 2026-11-04, so the band is about 34 times looser (spec 0044 §9). (3) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact calls `reconstructStaged (createMathNetSvd ()) MuellerReference.excludedPoints (opticsMuellerCaptures ())`, an `Error` failing the fact with its `%A`, and deletes every binding of its body that is neither an assertion nor its formatting (the stage-1 call of step 349, `airRowsOf`, `fitAirGain`, `meanTime`, `splitTime`, `day1Start`, `day1End`, `calibration`, `day1Cal`, `prepareRow`, `families` and `reconstructKind`); `worstElementDeviation` and `describeDeviation` stay. Its assertions read `staged.qz`, `staged.lr` and `staged.qzLr` (rank 16 each; the matrices within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol`), and its cascade check reads `cascadeProduct staged.lr.matrix staged.qz.matrix` until step 352. It gains one assertion that reports all nine deviations, as the matrix assertion does: each AIR gain of `staged.gains` (`lpLp.gainA`, `lpLp.gainB`, `lpCpl.gainA`, `lpCpl.gainB`, `cplLp.gainPre`, `cplLp.gainPost` and the `Day2Single` gain of `cplCpl`, a `Day1Interp` failing the fact) and of `staged.cplCplDay1Gain` (`gainStart`, `gainEnd`) is within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of its `MuellerReference` value. Its leading comment says, in one to three lines, that it runs the promoted staged path (spec 0050 S10.3) over the kit's lab files; its spec 0044 §8.4 and §8.5 paragraphs keep their text, and the comments of the moved code go with it. (4) Tests, in `StagedMuellerPathTests` (step 349), over test-local synthetic captures whose AIR rows are, per label, nine readings at 0°, 20°, …, 160° with `avgTotal` 2 + cos 2α at fixed literal times, one darkness row and one bullshit-check row, so stage 1 solves: `the staged path answers a typed error naming an AIR block that holds no capture row`: the LP-LP, LP-CPL and CPL-LP files hold only their first block (`LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2`) and the day files nothing, so `reconstructStaged` answers `EmptyCaptureSetErr` whose reason holds `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R`; `the staged path answers a typed error naming the object whose solve fails`: all nine blocks and no science row answer `ObjectReconstructionErr (Qz, SingularDesignErr _)`, the empty QZ design reaching the real `createMathNetSvd ()`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the path computes every gain, projection and solve by the same float operations in the same order; a probe this spec ran at authoring through the same functions reproduced the summary's nine gains within 2.9e-11 and its row counts (QZ 228, LR 227, QZ+LR 228). The gain assertion compares values the fact already computes, and `MuellerReconstructionTests`' count is unchanged (001 §W: no new inverse-physics test).

**Acceptance.** After the staged path is promoted, `StagedMuellerPath.reconstructStaged` MUST answer the stage-1 constants, the nine AIR gains and M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} with their rank and residual, or a typed `StagedMuellerError`, and the section 7.2 fact MUST call it, hold only assertions and their formatting, and find every gain within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference`'s; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the staged path answers a typed error naming an AIR block that holds no capture row` and `the staged path answers a typed error naming the object whose solve fails`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.
